;; Configuration for the documentation site, read by the docs-engine
;; (https://github.com/b12n-oss/docs-engine).
;;
;; Build it locally with `bb site:serve`. CI builds it on every pull
;; request from .github/workflows/site.yml, and will publish from main
;; once both the PUBLISH_SITE repository variable is set to "true" and
;; GitHub Pages is enabled, neither of which is done yet.
{;; :base-path is what makes this a project site rather than an org one.
 ;; The site is served at https://b12n-oss.github.io/mcp-tkx/, so every
 ;; URL the engine emits needs that prefix. Leave it out and the pages
 ;; still render, but each one loads the ORGANIZATION site's stylesheet
 ;; and every asset 404s. The workflow has a check for exactly this.
 :base-path   "/mcp-tkx"

 :title       "mcp-tkx"
 :description "A Clojure and ClojureScript library for building Model Context Protocol clients and servers. Four protocol revisions, negotiated at the handshake, with kebab-case handlers over a camelCase wire."}
